WEBVTT

00:00:01.021 --> 00:00:12.899
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:18.605
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:18.605 --> 00:00:25.534
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.046 --> 00:00:37.082
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.257 --> 00:00:43.196
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.196 --> 00:00:50.602
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.373 --> 00:00:58.412
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:58.412 --> 00:01:05.285
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.285 --> 00:01:10.891
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:10.891 --> 00:01:17.164
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.164 --> 00:01:25.594
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:46.593 --> 00:01:50.689
Well, I guess they didn't try to
run away after all.

00:02:03.276 --> 00:02:08.009
THE PLACE I WANT TO GO

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.032
-Blast!
-Director!

00:02:26.032 --> 00:02:28.023
Director!

00:02:31.972 --> 00:02:34.007
Have you found them?

00:02:34.007 --> 00:02:36.877
No... It looks like they
took the train from Natsuna.

00:02:36.877 --> 00:02:39.579
Then get someone to intercept
them at the next station!

00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:41.069
I already did...

00:02:41.214 --> 00:02:43.580
Who am I in this institution?

00:02:44.284 --> 00:02:47.220
The director, of course.
What are you talking about?

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.984
Then put yourself in my place
and bring them back!

00:02:50.223 --> 00:02:52.282
Yes, Sir!

00:02:54.561 --> 00:02:56.563
This is Natsuna.

00:02:56.563 --> 00:03:00.066
But across the bridge is Wattfort,
then Saint-Remi.

00:03:00.066 --> 00:03:02.436
And from there it's
the Western Mainland.

00:03:02.436 --> 00:03:05.166
After that we'll just keep
going as far as we can.

00:03:08.508 --> 00:03:10.677
Are you thirsty?

00:03:10.677 --> 00:03:13.544
Or do you want something to eat?

00:03:15.248 --> 00:03:17.614
I took these from the orphanage.

00:03:20.086 --> 00:03:22.656
That's right, we still have a long way to go.

00:03:22.656 --> 00:03:24.681
I'll save mine for later, too.

00:03:36.102 --> 00:03:39.333
Where do you suppose that place is?

00:03:42.342 --> 00:03:44.367
I don't know...

00:03:46.847 --> 00:03:50.283
I've been trying to figure it out but...

00:03:51.251 --> 00:03:54.277
I don't know either.

00:03:55.355 --> 00:03:57.186
But...

00:03:57.891 --> 00:03:59.926
Oh.

00:03:59.926 --> 00:04:02.963
Don't worry!
You'll remember someday.

00:04:02.963 --> 00:04:06.296
It must be an important place
to you, Helga.

00:04:10.937 --> 00:04:15.431
I am lost and burning
in the desert of human life.

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:20.543
And I groan under the
heavy burden I carry.

00:04:20.614 --> 00:04:24.914
But somewhere, there is an
almost forgotten blossoming,

00:04:24.985 --> 00:04:29.684
in a garden of cool shadows.
I know it.

00:04:30.323 --> 00:04:34.127
However, in a place so far
away it seems like dream,

00:04:34.127 --> 00:04:38.723
a resting place is waiting.
I know it.

00:04:39.466 --> 00:04:42.335
My soul will once again have a home,

00:04:42.335 --> 00:04:46.567
a place where rest and
night and stars are waiting...

00:04:48.174 --> 00:04:49.641
That's Hesse, right?

00:04:49.743 --> 00:04:53.008
That man understood
the true meaning of pain.

00:04:55.415 --> 00:05:00.148
I wonder if we'll be able
to find that place, too?

00:05:03.423 --> 00:05:07.587
We're just like this pathetic, slow train,
we can never manage to get there.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.400
-When will we?
-We'll definitely make it back.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.804
-That's why we're searching for Tina!
-What if we don't find her?

00:05:17.804 --> 00:05:21.808
-Will we receive a prize like Palza did?
-Hesma!

00:05:21.808 --> 00:05:25.471
The scientific advancement within
the past 100 years has been remarkable.

00:05:25.545 --> 00:05:27.747
Don't you agree?

00:05:27.747 --> 00:05:32.013
But those sudden, drastic changes
don't bode well for the future.

00:05:32.218 --> 00:05:34.311
What do you mean?

00:05:35.622 --> 00:05:38.386
It was Palza who made
that advancement possible!

00:05:42.162 --> 00:05:46.064
It will create a ripple effect,
like throwing a pebble into a pond.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.636
-Is this the Cole residence?
-Who are you?

00:06:56.636 --> 00:07:00.163
My name is Cooks.
I'm with the state police.

00:07:01.007 --> 00:07:03.032
A detective?

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.449
I see...

00:07:09.449 --> 00:07:12.543
So it isn't that you've found Ian.

00:07:12.686 --> 00:07:17.824
No, communication between police
jurisdictions isn't the best.

00:07:17.824 --> 00:07:22.261
If the information about your
son had reached me earlier...

00:07:23.463 --> 00:07:26.626
That's Ian's younger sister.
Come here, Bel.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.030
Have you found my brother?

00:07:36.509 --> 00:07:40.080
So, what brings you here?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.516
What's been happening with
your son's case since then?

00:07:43.516 --> 00:07:46.419
3 years ago, they just called off.

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:49.877
They said that Ian left the house
of his own free will.

00:07:50.156 --> 00:07:52.992
Bel was only three years old then,

00:07:52.992 --> 00:07:55.729
the police used her statement
as a reason to end it.

00:07:55.729 --> 00:07:58.095
His sister was a witness?

00:07:58.298 --> 00:08:02.098
They said he simply ran away,
there was no sign of trouble or foul play.

00:08:02.168 --> 00:08:05.399
But he would never have
just run away like that.

00:08:06.072 --> 00:08:08.875
He disappeared 6 years ago...

00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:11.241
That was in 2006, right?

00:08:12.846 --> 00:08:15.515
Actually, that same year
there was a series of...

00:08:15.515 --> 00:08:18.541
disappearances of young children.

00:08:22.388 --> 00:08:25.084
All of them went missing
at the age of five.

00:08:32.398 --> 00:08:35.231
Is there a connection to Ian?

00:08:38.905 --> 00:08:42.466
This is a group called
the Children of Befort.

00:08:44.077 --> 00:08:46.146
Befort?

00:08:46.146 --> 00:08:49.274
This looks like a very old picture.

00:09:08.234 --> 00:09:11.004
This is a picture of Ian, isn't it?

00:09:11.004 --> 00:09:14.201
What do you think?
They look a lot alike.

00:09:33.092 --> 00:09:36.357
Are you saying that this is Ian?

00:09:37.997 --> 00:09:42.229
No, this picture was taken
more than 100 years ago.

00:09:43.036 --> 00:09:46.301
It can't possibly be him.

00:09:46.539 --> 00:09:49.133
Oh, I see.

00:09:50.043 --> 00:09:54.980
However, I can't help wondering
about this picture.

00:10:01.588 --> 00:10:05.649
Ian... was a very gentle boy.

00:10:05.892 --> 00:10:11.228
He was so kind it was
sometimes almost heartbreaking.

00:10:12.332 --> 00:10:15.790
He was a small 5 year old child,

00:10:15.969 --> 00:10:20.065
but he seemed so devoted
to us and always did his best.

00:10:20.907 --> 00:10:23.943
There was something about him...
Yes...

00:10:23.943 --> 00:10:28.581
It was as if he wanted to make the
most out of his time with the family.

00:10:28.581 --> 00:10:31.744
He was very mature in that way.

00:10:35.121 --> 00:10:37.783
Your tea's gone cold.

00:10:38.925 --> 00:10:41.661
Was Ian born with that hair color?

00:10:41.661 --> 00:10:45.498
No, he had the same chestnut color
as Bel when he was born.

00:10:45.498 --> 00:10:48.568
It gradually turned white.
I was told that...

00:10:48.568 --> 00:10:51.738
...in his great-grandfather's time
the family came here from Europe.

00:10:51.738 --> 00:10:54.969
So it must be from
that side of the family.

00:10:55.775 --> 00:11:00.269
Your brother told you he was
leaving all on his own, didn't he?

00:11:04.884 --> 00:11:09.446
It must have been hard for you.
I'm sure I'll find him for you.

00:11:12.926 --> 00:11:17.226
Bel, there's something I want to ask you.

00:11:17.697 --> 00:11:22.862
When your brother left the house,
were there any other children with him?

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:31.934
Children, who were probably around
the same age as your brother.

00:11:37.083 --> 00:11:41.520
I see. You remembered that
very well. Thank you.

00:11:42.155 --> 00:11:44.589
-What is it?
-Nothing.

00:11:51.631 --> 00:11:54.067
Wattfort, Wattfort.

00:11:54.067 --> 00:11:56.903
The train on track one will be
connecting with the express train...

00:11:56.903 --> 00:12:00.306
...bound for Ayuta on the
Western Mainland via Claremont.

00:12:00.306 --> 00:12:02.797
Please board the train
and await departure.

00:12:06.679 --> 00:12:08.781
Finally, the Western Mainland!

00:12:08.781 --> 00:12:11.517
I've never been to the
Western Mainland before.

00:12:11.517 --> 00:12:15.146
It's really big, so hopefully,
that place will be there, Helga!

00:12:16.022 --> 00:12:20.186
Hey, Chitto. Sorry to bother you
when you're having fun!

00:12:28.167 --> 00:12:32.105
G-Good morning! Are you guys going
on vacation or something?

00:12:32.105 --> 00:12:34.573
Don't play dumb,
you little brat!!

00:13:25.425 --> 00:13:27.757
It's starting to rain!

00:13:33.032 --> 00:13:36.331
Come on, everyone get inside!

00:13:39.238 --> 00:13:41.207
Hey, the bus is coming!

00:13:41.207 --> 00:13:43.471
You're right. I wonder why?

00:13:46.646 --> 00:13:49.182
-Okay, get off!
-It's Chitto!

00:13:49.182 --> 00:13:51.912
-Guess he ran away again.
- Helga's with him too. They never learn.

00:13:52.018 --> 00:13:54.418
-Come on, Helga.
-Chitto, what're you doing?!

00:13:54.487 --> 00:13:58.218
-She'll get wet!
-Just get in the school!

00:14:10.236 --> 00:14:11.737
What now?!

00:14:11.737 --> 00:14:13.840
It must be tough having to
stay there all the time.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.808
Whose fault is that?!

00:14:15.808 --> 00:14:18.743
-Excuse me.
-Just go write your apology!

00:14:28.387 --> 00:14:31.151
What's the matter?
You haven't written anything.

00:14:31.491 --> 00:14:34.193
You only just came here and
you've run away 3 times.

00:14:34.193 --> 00:14:37.094
You snuck aboard the
supply boat, got on a train,

00:14:37.163 --> 00:14:40.223
and then you didn't have enough
money to get to Wattfort.

00:14:40.299 --> 00:14:43.462
You've broken countless rules.

00:14:44.036 --> 00:14:47.369
My dependability as the director
of this institution comes into question.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:49.874
All because of your selfishness.

00:14:52.545 --> 00:14:54.945
You're not repentant at all?

00:14:56.149 --> 00:14:58.674
Do you hate this place so much?

00:15:01.921 --> 00:15:05.049
I just don't seem to be
getting through to you.

00:15:09.595 --> 00:15:13.326
You're much more stubborn
than you look.

00:15:14.534 --> 00:15:18.937
But in order to live here
you need to be more obedient.

00:15:19.505 --> 00:15:23.100
I'm not like the director
from your last children's home.

00:15:23.676 --> 00:15:27.806
It's the director's job to
properly manage the children.

00:15:28.881 --> 00:15:31.984
You're not leaving here until
you finish writing your apology.

00:15:31.984 --> 00:15:33.975
Understand?

00:15:34.387 --> 00:15:36.956
Oh, yes. It's been decided that Chitto...

00:15:36.956 --> 00:15:38.624
will be transferred to another orphanage.

00:15:38.624 --> 00:15:42.116
I've had enough of your nonsense.

00:16:07.019 --> 00:16:09.388
Helga! Helga!

00:16:09.388 --> 00:16:11.686
Behave yourself, Chitto!

00:16:12.391 --> 00:16:15.328
The director has made his decision.
Give it up, Chitto.

00:16:15.328 --> 00:16:18.126
Now let's go!
Geez, don't be such a pain!

00:16:19.465 --> 00:16:22.434
-Chitto! That brat!
-Helga!

00:16:24.403 --> 00:16:26.462
Helga!

00:16:29.709 --> 00:16:32.712
What are you guys doing?!
Just get him out of here!

00:16:32.712 --> 00:16:36.409
How are we going to explain to the
welfare department if he escapes again?

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:47.193
Cardiac arrest!
Passing threw red sector!

00:16:47.193 --> 00:16:49.829
-1 minute 40 seconds! 2 minutes!
-Brain area immeasurable!

00:16:49.829 --> 00:16:51.764
Tracking in black sector!

00:16:51.764 --> 00:16:54.000
Thirty, fifty-eight!!
One minute twenty!

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.991
Professor, please look at this!

00:16:56.402 --> 00:16:57.970
-W-What happened?!
-Professor!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.372
Swelling detected in the brain stem!

00:16:59.372 --> 00:17:01.340
It's radiation!
Intensity 150000 stilb!

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:04.571
Bring him back immediately!
Abort! Abort operation!

00:17:09.949 --> 00:17:13.908
It's really raining hard. I wonder
if I'll be able to go pick up Mom?

00:17:27.767 --> 00:17:29.702
Are you suicidal?!
Idiot!!

00:17:29.702 --> 00:17:33.005
You're just going to crash into
the island going that fast.

00:17:33.005 --> 00:17:35.441
Don't be so down, Chitto.

00:17:35.441 --> 00:17:38.778
If you miss Helga, you can always
come visit once in a while.

00:17:38.778 --> 00:17:41.747
I'm sure even the director
would let you do that.

00:17:42.782 --> 00:17:44.773
What's wrong?

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:47.785
-It's a boat! We're going to hit!
-Idiot!

00:17:50.089 --> 00:17:52.387
Now he's done it.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:58.097
Y-Yes, that's right.
We need an emergency rescue!

00:17:58.097 --> 00:18:01.267
What?! The other boat?!
How should I know?!

00:18:01.267 --> 00:18:03.997
It just went racing off!

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.404
Hey, Chitto, you alright? Chitto?

00:18:08.974 --> 00:18:11.444
-Oh, no! Chitto's gone!
-What?!

00:18:11.444 --> 00:18:13.312
He must have fallen overboard
when we hit!

00:18:13.312 --> 00:18:17.476
-He must still be around somewhere!
-Chitto! Chitto!

00:18:20.252 --> 00:18:22.652
I wonder if they're alright?

00:18:23.689 --> 00:18:26.681
Hey, moron, we meet again.

00:18:27.026 --> 00:18:28.926
Chitto!

00:18:30.696 --> 00:18:32.531
Visibility was poor and
there was an accident.

00:18:32.531 --> 00:18:35.159
He was knocked overboard
and hasn't been found.

00:18:35.801 --> 00:18:41.569
If Chitto really is dead, I'm going to
face some kind of punishment.

00:18:41.841 --> 00:18:44.867
And it's all your fault, Helga!

00:18:55.454 --> 00:18:58.855
So you guys are always
trying to run away?

00:18:59.558 --> 00:19:01.427
Here you go!

00:19:01.427 --> 00:19:06.732
Well... I just want to take Helga
to the place she wants to go to.

00:19:06.732 --> 00:19:09.997
Helga? That girl's name is Helga?

00:19:10.803 --> 00:19:13.539
Don't go saying her name
like you know her, uh...

00:19:13.539 --> 00:19:16.337
-I'm Thoma.
-Thoma?

00:19:16.442 --> 00:19:18.411
That guy in the glasses
is the director, right?

00:19:18.411 --> 00:19:21.346
He came to my house, too.
He's kind of creepy.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:25.248
Helga's really quiet,
so they always pick on her.

00:19:30.589 --> 00:19:33.683
I knew it, she's being picked on.

00:19:33.759 --> 00:19:35.995
Bye, Thoma. Thanks.

00:19:35.995 --> 00:19:39.398
H-Hey, Chitto.
Where are you going?

00:19:39.398 --> 00:19:42.168
-I have to go get Helga out.
-Hold on.

00:19:42.168 --> 00:19:45.471
It's still raining out there.
Hold on a second.

00:19:45.471 --> 00:19:48.338
Thoma? I'm glad you're still there.

00:19:48.474 --> 00:19:51.310
Yes, it's the rain.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:53.646
I'll be staying at a friend's house tonight.

00:19:53.646 --> 00:19:54.947
Right! I gotcha.

00:19:54.947 --> 00:19:57.848
-Tell your father for me!
-Okay!

00:19:58.584 --> 00:20:01.178
-That was a wireless from mom.
-Wireless?

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:03.522
There are no phones
on this island.

00:20:03.522 --> 00:20:06.091
Chitto, I'm going to go, too!

00:20:06.091 --> 00:20:09.061
A rowboat is useless in this rain.

00:20:09.061 --> 00:20:12.064
Even if you do get Helga out,
you'll be caught again in no time.

00:20:12.064 --> 00:20:14.400
We'll use my boat to get onto Chikao!

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.425
-Really?!
-Yup!

00:20:17.002 --> 00:20:19.470
Now that that's decided...

00:20:24.076 --> 00:20:27.546
What's with him?!
Nobody can sleep this early!

00:20:27.546 --> 00:20:30.174
Hey, Thoma! Hey!

00:21:00.513 --> 00:21:02.310
What's that?

00:21:04.083 --> 00:21:06.847
Hey! Wake up! Chitto! Hey!

00:21:06.986 --> 00:21:10.922
-Have you noticed anything?
-Nothing in particular.

00:21:14.393 --> 00:21:16.095
Who were those guys?

00:21:16.095 --> 00:21:18.464
They're looking for some
escaped criminals.

00:21:18.464 --> 00:21:21.400
Apparently they're hiding out
somewhere around here.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.669
-Escaped criminals?
-Some men and women.

00:21:23.669 --> 00:21:25.738
They escaped by boat.

00:21:25.738 --> 00:21:27.729
By boat?

00:21:29.108 --> 00:21:31.633
Come on, Thoma.
Let's have something to eat.

00:21:32.778 --> 00:21:36.043
Hey, Chitto! Come on out!
It's alright!

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.453
Father, this is my friend.

00:21:41.453 --> 00:21:43.689
I'm Chitto... Nice to meet you.

00:21:43.689 --> 00:21:46.425
He's from Chikao. There was
something he needed to do...

00:21:46.425 --> 00:21:49.128
I'm taking him back tomorrow morning.

00:21:49.128 --> 00:21:51.392
I see, your friend?

00:21:52.197 --> 00:21:55.000
Well, just don't go outside
in the middle of the night, okay?

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.663
Don't worry!
Come on! Let's eat, Chitto!

00:22:05.945 --> 00:22:09.381
See, ten on the dot!
He's going to the temple.

00:22:09.381 --> 00:22:11.781
Okay! Let's go, Chitto!

00:22:36.508 --> 00:22:46.315
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:46.919 --> 00:22:55.861
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:55.861 --> 00:23:00.594
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:23:00.833 --> 00:23:05.668
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:06.271 --> 00:23:15.407
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:16.015 --> 00:23:21.086
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:21.086 --> 00:23:25.791
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:25.791 --> 00:23:30.194
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:30.796 --> 00:23:35.100
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:39.969
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
